  "text": "That sounds like a thoughtful and delicious idea! A classic breakfast omelette is a great choice for a surprise breakfast in bed \u2014 it's simple, satisfying, and can be customized to your mom's tastes. Here's a step-by-step guide to making a classic omelette:\n\n### **Classic Breakfast Omelette Recipe**\n\n**Ingredients:**\n- 3 large eggs\n- 1/4 cup (about 2 tablespoons) milk or cream (optional, for fluffiness)\n- Salt and pepper to taste\n- 1/2 teaspoon butter or oil (for cooking)\n- Optional fillings: cheese, herbs, cooked bacon, ham, avocado, mushrooms, spinach, etc.\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. **Crack the eggs into a mixing bowl.** Add the milk or cream if using, and season with salt and pepper. Whisk until the mixture is smooth and frothy.\n\n2. **Heat a non-stick skillet over medium heat.** Add the butter or oil and let it melt.\n\n3. **Pour the egg mixture into the skillet.** Let it cook undisturbed for about 2-3 minutes, or until the edges are set and the center is still slightly runny.\n\n4. **Use a spatula to gently lift the edges of the omelette and let the uncooked edges cook.** This helps create a fluffier texture.\n\n5. **Once the omelette is almost set, gently flip it using a spatula to cook the other side for another 1-2 minutes.**\n\n6. **Add your favorite fillings.** If using cheese, sprinkle it over one half of the omelette before folding. You can also add cooked bacon, ham, spinach, or avocado.\n\n7. **Fold the omelette in half and let it rest for a minute to allow the fillings to meld and the cheese to melt.**\n\n8. **Serve warm, and enjoy your mom\u2019s breakfast in bed!**\n\n**Pro Tip:** For a richer flavor, you can substitute some of the milk with cream or even a splash of vanilla extract for a sweet twist.\n\nLet me know if you want to add a special touch, like a side of toast or fresh fruit \u2014 or if you want to make it vegan or gluten-free!",
